# Screen: Firewall (main menu 4) 2 (Configure firewall), ufw inactive, sshd_config holding Port 22 (pkg/menu), run in a child process
# Script: stdin "2\n\n", not a terminal, so nothing typed is echoed
# Start: Debian 13; ufw inactive, no rules; cfg.SshPort 2230; 0 profiles; dryRun false
# Pauses: 1 ("Press Enter to ..."; origin/main says "Press any key to ...", DEV-050)
# KNOWN-DEFECT: V9: ufw default, ufw disable and ufw reset run before the allow rule, and only cfg.SshPort is allowed, not the effective sshd port. The sshd_config seeded here says 22 and is not read: on this host the sequence would leave 22 closed. Item 1 and item 2 take no confirmation: disable, reset and the enable run on the one key (firewall_menu.go:210-227, :263). Only disabling asks, and disabling is a stub.
# NOTE: "Default policy" and "SSH allowed" under the success line are printed from cfg and constants, not read back from ufw (firewall_menu.go:272-273).
